# CORRECTED 2026-08-19. The earlier header claimed this project was LOCAL-ONLY
# with no git repository. That was WRONG: a git repository DOES exist and covers
# this project. These rules are LIVE - they decide what actually gets committed.
#
# Separate standing rule: Claude must not run or suggest ANY git command.

# Secrets - never commit these.
.env
automation/.bottomline_session.json

# The virtual environment and the browser Playwright downloads.
.venv/
.browsers/

# Run logs may contain vendor names and invoice numbers.
logs/

# Recorded field captures may reveal client system internals.
# The wildcard also covers selectors_recorded.run1-15fields.json, which must
# stay ON DISK (it is the evidence behind the field map) but must never be
# committed. Note: selectors.json - the hand-built map - is NOT ignored.
automation/selectors_recorded*.json

# Client data. The work list holds real vendor names and invoice numbers, and
# the screenshots are pictures of a live client system.
input/*.xlsx
notes/**/*.png

# Vendor/Property master data - real vendor names, addresses, ERP IDs and the
# whole property list. The source workbook AND everything flattened out of it
# (masters/vendors.csv, the alias file, etc.) are CLIENT DATA. Never commit.
Vendor&PropertyMaster.xlsx
masters/

# Invoice PDFs the reader (invoice_reader.py) ingests. They live in a subfolder
# (input/pdfs/), which the root's `**/input/*.pdf` does NOT match, so guard them
# here. Every PDF is a client document -- never commit one.
input/**/*.pdf

# Claude Code's own folder - settings, skills, local permissions.
.claude/

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
